<title>GERMANY: EMI chief - chance of punctual EMU well above 50 pct.</title>
<headline>EMI chief - chance of punctual EMU well above 50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute (EMI) President Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Tuesday that he believed the chances of European monetary union starting on time were well above 50 percent.</p>
<p>Asked to comment on the likelihood of the project going ahead as scheduled on January 1, 1999, Lamfalussy said, &quot;In politics or economic life there is no such thing as 100 percent certainty.&quot;</p>
<p>But he added that he saw the chances as being &quot;significantly above 50 percent.&quot;</p>
<p>Lamfalussy was speaking at the launch of the European Central Bank forerunner's third annual report.</p>
</text>
